## Symptom

Found during B309 work (2026-09-18, L3 group). The subscribe-daemon IPC client verbs (`register` / `deregister` / `list` / `shutdown` in `ocaml/cli/c2c_relay_subscribe_daemon.ml`) double-close their socket fd on exit: `Lwt_io.close` on the channel followed by `Lwt_unix.close` on the fd. The second close raises EBADF, and the process exits **125** after an otherwise successful request/response exchange.

## Impact

Any caller that checks exit status (scripts, monitors, the new B309 `send_shutdown_best_effort` paths if they ever surface the code) sees failure after the command actually worked. Exit 125 is also the `timeout`-reserved code, which misleads triage.

## Fix direction

Close once: either close the Lwt_io channel (which owns the fd) or the fd directly — not both. Wrap in a best-effort `try ... with Unix_error _ -> ()` for the already-closed case if defensive.

## Evidence

Observed while writing `test_c2c_relay_b309_disable_consumers.ml`; pre-existing, deliberately out of B309 scope (B309 landed the shutdown sender bounded and non-raising, so the CLI surface is unaffected; the raw IPC verbs still misreport).

Lane plan 2026-09-18 (bl-fix-many B341 B342): two parallel lanes, disjoint files — B341 in .worktrees/b341-ipc (c2c_relay_subscribe_daemon.ml), B342 in .worktrees/b342-ca (c2c_relay_connector.ml inline client). No dependency; both from master tip 86ffa242.